UNIT isObjectLike
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG isObjectLike(value: any) -> boolean

DEPENDS-ON none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEHAVIOR  (single-expression pure predicate; no branches beyond the && )
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BEHAVIOR
  # The unit is a one-line pure predicate. EXACT source expression (verified
  # against the installed package, see PROVENANCE):
  #
  #     return !!value && typeof value == 'object';
  #
  # Re-emit this EXACT expression. Two sub-tests, evaluated left-to-right with
  # JS short-circuit semantics:
  #
  # NODE 1  truthiness gate:  !!value
  #   - `!!value` coerces `value` to a boolean via JS ToBoolean.
  #   - FALSE (short-circuits, predicate returns false) when value is any
  #     FALSY value: null, undefined, 0, -0, NaN, '' (empty string), false,
  #     0n (bigint zero).  (Also document.all in browsers — NOT reachable in
  #     Node; out of envelope, see SCOPE.)
  #   - TRUE (proceeds to NODE 2) for every truthy value, which includes
  #     EVERY object reference (all objects are truthy in JS, even wrapper
  #     objects of falsy primitives such as new Number(0), new String(''),
  #     new Boolean(false), and Object.create(null)).
  #
  # NODE 2  type gate:  typeof value == 'object'
  #   - Uses loose equality `==` against the string literal 'object'
  #     (behaviorally identical to `===` here since typeof always yields a
  #     string; re-emit `==` to match source exactly).
  #   - TRUE when JS `typeof value` is exactly the string "object".
  #     typeof yields "object" for: plain objects, arrays, Date, RegExp,
  #     Map, Set, WeakMap, WeakSet, typed arrays (Uint8Array etc.), Buffer,
  #     ArrayBuffer, Error, Promise, class instances, boxed-primitive wrapper
  #     objects (new Number/String/Boolean), Object(Symbol(...)), and null
  #     (typeof null === "object" — but null is excluded at NODE 1).
  #   - FALSE when typeof is anything else: "number", "string", "boolean",
  #     "bigint", "symbol", "undefined", "function".
  #
  # RESULT = NODE1 && NODE2.  Returns a primitive boolean (true | false).
  # No throw paths: the function never throws for any input (no property
  # access, no coercion that can fault).  No side effects (read-only).
  #
  # EQUIVALENCE NOTE (informational, do NOT change the emitted expression):
  #   `!!value` is behaviorally equivalent to `value != null` UNDER the NODE 2
  #   guard, because the ONLY falsy value whose typeof is "object" is null, and
  #   null is rejected by both. Every other object is truthy. Verified: no
  #   divergence across all reachable Node inputs. The teaching expression in
  #   the upstream lodash docs prose says "not null and typeof object"; the
  #   actual code uses `!!value`. Re-emit `!!value` to be byte-faithful to
  #   source; either form passes the oracle.

ORACLE value -> oracle.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXACT TRUE / FALSE EDGE SET  (self-consistent with genInputs curated prefix)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every value the generator can emit has its result fixed here.
#
# TRUE  (truthy AND typeof === "object"):
#   {}                      -> true   # plain object
#   { a: 1, nested:{...} }  -> true   # populated plain object
#   Object.create(null)     -> true   # null-prototype object (still typeof object, truthy)
#   []                      -> true   # empty array
#   [1,2,3]                 -> true   # populated array
#   new Date()              -> true
#   /x/  (RegExp)           -> true
#   new Map()               -> true
#   new Set()               -> true
#   new Uint8Array(n)       -> true   # typed array
#   Buffer.alloc(n)         -> true   # node Buffer (subclass of Uint8Array)
#   new Number(1)           -> true   # boxed number wrapper OBJECT (truthy)
#   new Number(0)           -> true   # boxed wrapper of falsy primitive is STILL truthy
#   new String('a')         -> true
#   new String('')          -> true   # boxed wrapper of '' is STILL truthy
#   new Boolean(true)       -> true
#   new Boolean(false)      -> true   # boxed wrapper of false is STILL truthy
#   class instance          -> true
#   Object(Symbol('s'))     -> true   # wrapped symbol object
#
# FALSE  (falsy at NODE 1, OR typeof !== "object"):
#   null                    -> false  # falsy (and would pass typeof, but rejected by NODE 1)
#   undefined               -> false  # falsy; typeof "undefined"
#   0                       -> false  # falsy; typeof "number"
#   -0                      -> false  # falsy; typeof "number"
#   1                       -> false  # truthy but typeof "number"
#   3.14                    -> false  # typeof "number"
#   NaN                     -> false  # falsy; typeof "number"
#   Infinity                -> false  # typeof "number"
#   -Infinity               -> false  # typeof "number"
#   ''  (empty string)      -> false  # falsy; typeof "string"
#   'a' (non-empty string)  -> false  # truthy but typeof "string"
#   true                    -> false  # typeof "boolean"
#   false                   -> false  # falsy; typeof "boolean"
#   1n  (bigint)            -> false  # typeof "bigint"
#   0n  (bigint zero)       -> false  # falsy; typeof "bigint"
#   function(){}            -> false  # typeof "function"  (OUT-OF-ENVELOPE codec; see SCOPE)
#   () => {}                -> false  # typeof "function"  (OUT-OF-ENVELOPE codec)
#   Symbol('s')             -> false  # typeof "symbol"    (OUT-OF-ENVELOPE codec)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE
  IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly):
    The whole unit. A single pure expression `!!value && typeof value == 'object'`.
    Reproduce both the truthiness gate and the loose-`==` typeof "object" test.
    Returns a primitive boolean. Never throws. No side effects.

  CARRIED DATA: none. No literal tables, no constants beyond the string "object".

  OUT-OF-CONTRACT: none (no stateful mutators, no side APIs, no ambient seam).
    The function reads nothing ambient — no clock/RNG/env/fs/net. It is a
    pure deterministic predicate of its single argument. Side-effect ledger N/A.

  OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (SPECIFIED behavior the inputs codec cannot serialize for
  cross-process emission — a blind re-emitter still reproduces these from this
  spec; genInputs does NOT emit them):
    - functions (any kind: declaration, arrow, async, generator, class
      constructors referenced as callable) -> typeof "function" -> FALSE.
    - Symbols (Symbol('x'), well-known symbols) -> typeof "symbol" -> FALSE.
      (NOTE: a *wrapped* symbol Object(Symbol('x')) IS typeof "object" -> TRUE,
       and that wrapper is also not round-trippable, so likewise out-of-envelope
       on the TRUE side.)
    - document.all (HTMLAllCollection): historically falsy with typeof either
      "object" or "undefined" depending on engine -> would be FALSE here via the
      `!!value` gate. NOT reachable in Node; informational only.

  CODEC NOTES for genInputs (which values round-trip vs not):
    Round-trips through JSON.stringify(encode(args)): plain objects, arrays,
    RegExp, Set, Map, Uint8Array/Buffer, bigint, JSON primitives
    (number incl. via special handling for NaN/+-Infinity/-0, string, boolean,
    null), undefined. Boxed primitives (new Number/String/Boolean) and class
    instances generally do NOT survive identity-preserving round-trip; the
    generator therefore exercises the boxed-wrapper TRUE path with PLAIN objects
    that share the same observable predicate result (typeof "object", truthy),
    and the SIR above pins the boxed-wrapper results so a blind engineer who
    reconstructs them by spec still matches. genInputs only emits codec-faithful
    values; non-round-trippable cases are documented OUT-OF-ENVELOPE above.

